What is it?
-----------

Simple. Its a tagline adder for CNet only.

What? Another one!
------------------

Yep :)

Huh? Okay then...
-----------------

Okay, so now we know what it is.  Good.  Its coded using a mixture of Arexx
and compiled basic (blitz 2).  The blitz bit was needed to speed this thing
up when it generates the random tagline.  I've used some of Dotorans
Supertags tagfiles (hope you dont mind Dave) put them into one huge file
with 17861 taglines in it.  You could of course use one of your own or one
of the many tagfiles that are about.  Not much to doing this really.

Okay tell me how!
-----------------

Easy. If you intend to create your own make sure the format of the tagfile
is laid out as below.
 
Each tagline in the tagfile must fit on one line.  The first line MUST be
the number of taglines in the tagfile.  So if you have 3000 taglines in
your file the first line should read 3000.  All lines after that are the
taglines themselves. Save this file as tagfile in the De-tag directory.

If you are using an already created tagfile. Then as long as each tagline
is on one line all you need to do is make sure the first line reflects the
number of taglines in that file.

I hope you understand all that! If not take a look at the tagfile in the
De-Tag directory.

How do I install this thing?
----------------------------

Unpack the archive De-Tag.lha into pfiles:  IT MUST BE IN PFILES (it looks
for De-tag/tagfile in pfiles:) Otherwise it wont work.  Then you have to
edit the BBSTEXT file.

Line numbers 218 Mail
             299 Feedback
             400 Posting
             478 Responding

Can be altered. Which or all of these lines you use is entirely up to you.
Add to each of the lines you wish to alter like this...

{#0pfiles:De-Tag/De-Tag.rexx}
|
Control-Q (as you should know by now!)

If you alter all lines they should look like this....

218:    {#0pfiles:De-Tag/De-Tag.rexx}\n1Mail filing...
299:    {#0pfiles:De-Tag/De-Tag.rexx}\n1Feedback filing...
        |                            |
        |                            Control-Y
400:    {#0pfiles:De-Tag/De-Tag.rexx}Post filing...
478:    {#0pfiles:De-Tag/De-Tag.rexx}Response filing...
        |
        Control-Q

Painless no? Of course it was! :)

Its pretty quick. On my 030/50 A1200 it took about 2/3 seconds to get the
last tagline from the tagfile provided. How quick it is on yours will
obviously depend on your processor speed.

Thats about it!

